      "message": "fix(geometry): one smooth crease between curved faces is one feature edge\n\nThe face rule of feature::chains joins two edges only when they bound one\nplanar face. On a crease between a conical chamfer and a cylindrical wall\neach chord has a different planar strip on both sides, so the crease fell\napart into chord-long pieces (fig8.step: 719 runs, longest 17.22 mm).\n\nAdd the G1 seam rule (feature/g1_seam.rs): join two edges at a vertex\nwhen they separate the same two welded patches (or rim one open sheet),\nthe vertex has no other real feature edge, and the turn is at most\nCHAIN_TANGENT_DEG. The trail walk (feature/trail.rs, moved out of\nfeature.rs) keeps a joined pair consecutive. No point moves; no chord is\ndropped. fig8 lower rim: 10 runs, longest 188.49 mm.\n\nPins: crates/app/tests/feature_edge_g1_join.rs, with fig8.step as a new\nfixture.\n\nFixes #2209\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
